# Window names become tuitp-<name>. Default before the first --- is dev.
# Ordinary wtp-compatible folder rows open CMD with global + local senv.
--- dev
%USERPROFILE%\git\project-a|Ordinary project tab

# A TUIOS tab attaches to the FIRST session; use TUIOS's session switcher
# for the other sessions. Project sessions have Claude/Codex/CMD workspaces.
=== Projects
+ %USERPROFILE%\git\project-a|project-a
+ %USERPROFILE%\git\project-b|project-b

=== Test
+ %USERPROFILE%\git\test|test|single

# One pane: local senv.bat if present, otherwise global; then the chosen tool.
# + %USERPROFILE%\git\test|test-claude|claude
# + %USERPROFILE%\git\test|test-codex|codex
# + %USERPROFILE%\git\test|test-shell|senv
# 'single' is the backward-compatible spelling of 'senv'.

--- experiments
=== OSC-7501-Demo
+ %USERPROFILE%\git\tests\so\osc7501-demo|osc7501-demo|single

# Move an === block under another --- line to move its tab, retaining
# the TUIOS sessions. Removing a session entirely terminates its processes.
# Only previously managed sessions are removed; unrelated sessions survive.
# 'tuitp stop' closes every managed tab, deletes every TUIOS session and
# stops the TUIOS daemon, whatever this list declares; the next 'tuitp'
# recreates the sessions from it.
